stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    [*] --> Fetch: Reset PC = 0x00000000
    state "Instruction fetch" as Fetch {
        FETCH_REQ --> FETCH_WAIT: One-cycle memory response
    }
    Fetch --> Decode: Instruction received
    state "Decode" as Decode
    state "Execute" as Execute
    state "Writeback" as Writeback
    state "Halt" as Halt
    Decode --> Execute
    Execute --> Writeback: Other successful instructions
    Execute --> Memory: Load / store
    state "Memory access" as Memory {
        MEM_READ_REQ --> MEM_READ_WAIT: One-cycle data / fault response
        MEM_WRITE_REQ --> MEM_WRITE_WAIT: One-cycle fault response
    }
    Memory --> Writeback: Success
    Writeback --> Fetch: Commit PC / optional rd; retire
    Fetch --> Halt: Fetch fault
    Execute --> Halt: Execution trap
    Memory --> Halt: Access fault
    Halt --> Halt: Until reset
    Halt --> Fetch: Reset PC = 0x00000000
    note right of Memory
        Request accepted at edge N.
        Core consumes response at edge N+1.
        Valid stores commit at edge N.
    end note
